  "usage_note": "**Strengthen** is used both with an object (*Exercise strengthens the heart*) and without one (*The wind strengthened during the night*). The opposite is **weaken**. For a person who becomes stronger after an illness, *get stronger* is more common in everyday speech: *She is getting stronger every day*.",
  "learner_errors": [
    {
      "incorrect": "This player will stronger our team.",
      "correct": "This player will strengthen our team.",
      "note": "**Stronger** is an adjective; the verb is **strengthen**."
    },
    {
      "incorrect": "We need to strength the team.",
      "correct": "We need to strengthen the team.",
      "note": "**Strength** is a noun. The verb adds **-en**: **strengthen**."
    },
    {
      "incorrect": "We need to strenghten the wall.",
      "correct": "We need to strengthen the wall.",
      "note": "In the spelling, **g** comes before **th**: **streng** + **then**."
    }
